CM_ "Message database for the DAQ bus (the TIM's CAN2), ADR 0003.
CAN FD, 500 kbit/s arbitration, 2 Mbit/s data. Logging and display data only:
nothing on the Control bus waits on this bus and no safety function reads it.
Generated C: App/common/logic/can_db/can_daq.[ch], made by can/generate.py
and committed. Change a layout here, regenerate, commit both.

The ID plan is the one written in can/control.dbc; an ID means the same frame
on either bus. Used here: 0x280 and 0x290 (the 0x080 and 0x090 status frames
plus 0x200, in the medium data range) and 0x610-0x64F (slow pack detail).

Every frame is little-endian. Bits are numbered from bit 0 of byte 0. A bit or
byte with no signal is spare: sent as 0, ignored on receive. No frame has a
CRC or counter.

The pack frames come once per module, named <Name>_00 to <Name>_15 with evenly
spaced IDs. All sixteen copies of a frame must have the same layout:
can/generate.py refuses to run otherwise, and it generates C for the _00 copy
only. The firmware packs module n with the _00 code and sends it on the _00
ID plus n times the spacing. Modules count 0-15, cells and temperature
sensors 0-7 within a module.";

CM_ BU_ VCU "TIM running the VCU image. Records every DAQ bus frame in its Data log.";
CM_ BU_ BMS "TIM running the BMS image.";
CM_ BO_ 640 "Warnings from the BMS image that are not faults. Every 100 ms, from the DAQ publisher. Byte 0 and byte 1 bits, bytes 2-3 spare, bytes 4-7 Records dropped. Same layout in both images.";
CM_ SG_ 640 OverrunSeen "At least one Overrun since power-on.";
CM_ SG_ 640 BackgroundStalled "Housekeeping has not run for 1 s.";
CM_ SG_ 640 ControlBusState "State of the Control bus controller (CAN1).";
CM_ SG_ 640 CardState "State of the Data log card. Never a fault.";
CM_ SG_ 640 EventsDropped "An Event was dropped because the queue to the Event writer was full.";
CM_ SG_ 640 AllocationFailed "The failed-allocation hook has run.";
CM_ SG_ 640 RecordsDropped "Data log Records dropped at the ring since power-on.";
CM_ BO_ 656 "Warnings from the VCU image that are not faults. Every 100 ms, from the DAQ publisher. Byte 0 and byte 1 bits, bytes 2-3 spare, bytes 4-7 Records dropped. Same layout in both images.";
